				{
					"kind": "class",
					"name": "MemoryManager",
					"namespace": "Mowo",
					"doc": "Global frame arena. Bump-allocate scratch that dies within the frame;\nthe whole arena is reset at the frame boundary.\n\nThe thread that initialized the manager (the game thread) bumps the main\narena with no lock; every other thread bumps a chain of blocks of its own,\nalso with no lock. FrameAlloc used to take one process-wide mutex per call,\nso parallel systems serialized on their scratch. ResetFrameAllocator resets\nthem all, which is safe only at the frame boundary with no job in flight —\nthe guarantee the engine loop already gives.\n\nGAME-THREAD-FRAME SCOPED: the reset runs at the end of the game thread's\nloop with no render-thread flush on the no-overlay path, so under\nrender-ahead an allocation still referenced by the render thread's\nin-flight record job is reused underneath it. Render-path code must use\nplain heap containers, never FrameAlloc/FrameVector.",
					"line": 51,
